### Complexity Analysis
- **Time Complexity**: 
  - Constructor / Destructor: $\mathcal{O}(1)$ system heap boundary calls.
  - `allocate_bytes` / `allocate`: $\mathcal{O}(1)$ pure arithmetic pointer bumping with zero locking overhead or metadata scanning.
  - `reset`: $\mathcal{O}(1)$ single offset assignment back to zero.
- **Space Complexity**: $\mathcal{O}(C)$ where $C$ is the pre-allocated capacity size designated at arena construction time, guaranteeing zero dynamic fragmentation.

Here is a complete, thread-safe bounded MPMC queue implemented using atomic operations and an unsafe ring buffer with proper memory ordering.

```rust
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};
use std::cell::UnsafeCell;
use std::mem::MaybeUninit;
use std::sync::Arc;
use std::thread;

pub struct ConcurrentQueue<T> {
    buffer: Box<[UnsafeCell<MaybeUninit<T>>]>,
    capacity: usize,
    mask: usize,
    head: AtomicUsize,
    tail: AtomicUsize,
}

unsafe impl<T: Send> Sync for ConcurrentQueue<T> {}
unsafe impl<T: Send> Send for ConcurrentQueue<T> {}

impl<T> ConcurrentQueue<T> {
    pub fn new(capacity: usize) -> Self {
        assert!(capacity > 0 && (capacity & (capacity - 1)) == 0, "Capacity must be a power of two");
        let mut vec = Vec::with_capacity(capacity);
        for _ in 0..capacity {
            vec.push(UnsafeCell::new(MaybeUninit::uninit()));
        }
        Self {
            buffer: vec.into_boxed_slice(),
            capacity,
            mask: capacity - 1,
            head: AtomicUsize::new(0),
            tail: AtomicUsize::new(0),
        }
    }

    pub fn push(&self, value: T) -> Result<(), T> {
        let tail = self.tail.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
        loop {
            let head = self.head.load(Ordering::Acquire);
            if tail.wrapping_sub(head) >= self.capacity {
                return Err(value);
            }
            match self.tail.compare_exchange_weak(
                tail,
                tail.wrapping_add(1),
                Ordering::Release,
                Ordering::Relaxed,
            ) {
                Ok(_) => {
                    unsafe {
                        let cell = self.buffer[tail & self.mask].get();
                        (*cell).write(value);
                    }
                    return Ok(());
                }
                Err(current) => {
                    let _ = current;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    pub fn pop(&self) -> Option<T> {
        let head = self.head.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
        loop {
            let tail = self.tail.load(Ordering::Acquire);
            if head == tail {
                return None;
            }
            match self.head.compare_exchange_weak(
                head,
                head.wrapping_add(1),
                Ordering::Release,
                Ordering::Relaxed,
            ) {
                Ok(_) => {
                    unsafe {
                        let cell = self.buffer[head & self.mask].get();
                        return Some((*cell).assume_init_read());
                    }
                }
                Err(current) => {
                    let _ = current;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

impl<T> Drop for ConcurrentQueue<T> {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        while self.pop().is_some() {}
    }
}

fn main() {
    let q = Arc::new(ConcurrentQueue::new(4));
    let q1 = Arc::clone(&q);
    let handle = thread::spawn(move || {
        q1.push(42).unwrap();
    });
    handle.join().unwrap();
    assert_eq!(q.pop(), Some(42));
}
```

### Complexity Analysis
- **Time Complexity**: $O(1)$ amortized per push/pop operation due to atomic CAS loops.
- **Space Complexity**: $O(N)$ where $N$ is the fixed capacity of the queue buffer.

