## 2. Mathematical Memory Liveness Proof

Let $M$ be a memory block allocated at timestamp $t_1$ and freed at $t_2$. A concurrent reader $R$ accessing $M$ must guarantee that its liveness interval $[start_R, end_R]$ satisfies:

$$end_R < t_1' \quad \text{where } t_1' \text{ is the subsequent allocation timestamp of } M$$

